#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""netcheck — terminal network health monitor.

Continuously samples latency, jitter, packet loss, DNS, throughput, and site
reachability; renders a live dashboard with sparklines; logs every check to CSV.
Built for flaky networks — plane WiFi, hotspots, cafes, captive portals.

Requires macOS, Python 3.8+, and `ping` and `curl` in PATH. Uses only the
standard library otherwise — no pip install. Linux/Windows are not currently
supported (ping flags differ; gateway/WiFi probes are macOS-specific).
"""

